WEBVTT

00:00.940 --> 00:07.560
Serena, who is currently participating in the Tripokalon Master Class, has advanced to the semifinals together with Sana and Musavie.

00:01.980 --> 00:11.820
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:08.220 --> 00:10.850
Who will challenge Kalos Queen Elle?

00:11.390 --> 00:13.790
The decisive competition has now started.

00:14.250 --> 00:16.210
She just needs to win twice more to become Kalos Queen!

00:17.140 --> 00:21.550
Ah, they need to settle this quickly or my heart will not make it!

00:21.550 --> 00:24.860
Geez, bro! Who's participating in this, you or them?

00:24.860 --> 00:25.500
But...

00:26.000 --> 00:28.490
Go, Musashi, Nyarth, Pumpjin!

00:28.910 --> 00:31.010
Remember that hellish training!

00:31.500 --> 00:32.610
You guys can d-

00:32.840 --> 00:38.550
The semifinals and finals will consist of free performances where each Performer will use two Pokémon.

00:39.650 --> 00:42.340
Whatever, we just need to stand out the most, right?

00:43.890 --> 00:46.140
Serena, let's not leave any regrets.

00:47.250 --> 00:47.650
Nope!

00:48.540 --> 00:52.000
All right, may the semifinals begin!

00:56.320 --> 01:02.040
Elle VS Serena!
Open the Door to the Future!!

01:02.600 --> 01:04.030
All right, let's begin!

01:03.050 --> 01:12.930
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

01:03.050 --> 01:12.930
Z

01:04.280 --> 01:07.310
There will be no second chances: Only one will make it.

01:07.960 --> 01:09.610
Kicking things off will be...

01:09.610 --> 01:11.410
...Performer Musavie!

01:16.300 --> 01:17.770
Leech Seed!

01:23.890 --> 01:25.440
The winner...

01:25.790 --> 01:26.120
...will...

01:26.570 --> 01:26.910
...be...

01:27.250 --> 01:27.870
...<i>me</i>!

01:34.590 --> 01:35.680
Seed Bomb!

01:38.570 --> 01:40.170
Nyarth, Fury Swipes!

01:40.170 --> 01:41.150
All right!

01:47.370 --> 01:48.060
Finish!

01:49.910 --> 01:51.520
Good job, Musavie!

01:53.880 --> 01:55.340
All right, next up is...

01:55.950 --> 01:57.360
...Performer Sana!

01:57.740 --> 01:59.990
Treat us to a splendid show, s'il-vous-plaît!

02:02.920 --> 02:05.150
Fushigisou, Vine Whip!

02:06.070 --> 02:07.970
Flabebe, Fairy Wind!

02:18.110 --> 02:19.130
Vine Whip!

02:26.860 --> 02:28.040
Solar Beam!

02:28.670 --> 02:29.670
Moonblast!

02:36.370 --> 02:37.270
Finish!

02:38.480 --> 02:39.570
Good job, Sana!

02:39.850 --> 02:41.280
Sana is so cool!

02:41.490 --> 02:45.310
At this point, even one mistake will have major consequences on their score.

02:45.670 --> 02:47.240
This will be the final entry.

02:47.730 --> 02:50.880
There's only one group left on this stage that will determine the finalist.

02:51.550 --> 02:53.900
Now then, let's have her dance:

02:54.140 --> 02:56.140
Performer Serena!

02:58.210 --> 02:59.250
Go, Serena!

02:59.930 --> 03:00.920
Do your best!

03:03.120 --> 03:04.500
Stay calm, stay calm...

03:08.550 --> 03:10.770
Nymphia, Swift!

03:19.040 --> 03:20.290
Yancham, Stone Edge!

03:51.890 --> 03:52.990
Finish!

03:57.070 --> 03:58.300
Nymphia, thank you!

04:02.090 --> 04:03.190
That was awesome, Serena!

04:03.950 --> 04:05.140
She can do this!

04:05.480 --> 04:07.400
Considering this is such a big event, that was excellent!

04:11.640 --> 04:14.910
Now then, let's move on to the voting for the semifinals.

04:15.680 --> 04:17.410
Members of the audience, grab your PokéLumes...

04:18.220 --> 04:20.370
...and those watching on TV, push the buttons!

04:20.730 --> 04:23.750
Then, please vote in accordance with the colors of the Performers!

04:24.550 --> 04:25.120
All right,

04:25.730 --> 04:26.250
please begin!

04:26.690 --> 04:27.200
Go!

04:27.200 --> 04:28.120
Please, just this once...

04:40.770 --> 04:46.720
Out of all the many Performers, Kalos Queen Elle's challenger has now been chosen!

04:50.030 --> 04:52.240
Serena, it's you!

04:53.930 --> 04:54.780
We did it...

04:55.650 --> 04:56.210
I really...

04:56.650 --> 04:57.350
...made it...

04:59.450 --> 05:01.320
Thank you, both of you!

05:01.520 --> 05:02.960
You did it, Serena!

05:02.960 --> 05:04.910
Eureka's happy, so happy!

05:04.910 --> 05:06.530
It is like I am dreaming!

05:06.930 --> 05:08.360
Well done.

05:08.360 --> 05:09.780
That's my daughter for you.

05:10.170 --> 05:13.410
Hey, that girl is my daughter, my pride and joy!

05:16.300 --> 05:17.820
Th-This is bad.

05:21.090 --> 05:23.450
Well, I made it this far.

05:24.240 --> 05:28.010
The Kalos folks should be aware of my beauty now.

05:29.820 --> 05:31.010
Serena, congratulations.

05:31.760 --> 05:34.770
Can <i>I</i> entrust my dream to you, too?

05:35.440 --> 05:36.000
Sana...

05:37.020 --> 05:39.710
I'd be lying if I said I wasn't sad, but...

05:42.950 --> 05:44.870
...please do your best on behalf of everyone that lost as well...

05:45.560 --> 05:47.830
You were more amazing than anyone else here, after all...

05:49.390 --> 05:49.660
I will.

05:52.360 --> 05:55.830
Please wait here. I'll call you when it's time.

05:56.410 --> 05:56.960
Okay.

06:06.080 --> 06:08.620
It's fine. There's no need to make this big a deal out of it.

06:11.480 --> 06:12.720
Uh, please come in.

06:19.450 --> 06:20.610
Show me.

06:21.670 --> 06:22.300
I mean your injury.

06:23.730 --> 06:24.480
How did you...?

06:24.880 --> 06:26.070
I could tell from your movements.

06:28.300 --> 06:30.240
You can barely make a fist.

06:31.110 --> 06:32.410
Withdraw from the finals.

06:33.160 --> 06:35.370
You won't be able to put on a decent performance like this,

06:36.200 --> 06:38.040
much less win against Elle.

06:41.920 --> 06:42.470
It's my...

06:43.160 --> 06:44.890
It's <i>our</i> dream.

06:45.790 --> 06:47.980
I had nothing, but then I finally...

06:48.670 --> 06:49.970
...found this dream together with my Pokémon.

06:51.890 --> 06:52.930
Now that we've made it this far,

06:53.750 --> 06:55.510
I don't want to give up till the end!

06:57.790 --> 06:59.900
I don't want to give up till the end!

07:01.120 --> 07:03.510
Geez, will the similarities ever end...?

07:05.080 --> 07:06.240
One performance only.

07:07.630 --> 07:09.500
I'll make sure it will hold for that.

07:11.930 --> 07:13.510
Once it's over, let a doctor examine you.

07:15.800 --> 07:16.130
All right!

07:18.270 --> 07:23.520
The très bien moment in which two Performers will fight for the glory of being Kalos Queen is finally here.

07:24.110 --> 07:27.300
Both can use as many Pokémon as they like...

07:27.670 --> 07:30.380
...and will perform at their absolute best!

07:31.590 --> 07:32.870
Competing in the finals will be...

07:33.240 --> 07:34.800
...Challenger Serena,

07:36.400 --> 07:38.170
as well as the current Queen,

07:38.890 --> 07:40.390
Performer Elle!

07:44.380 --> 07:45.080
That look on her face...

07:46.140 --> 07:47.350
Someone with this much resolve...

07:47.860 --> 07:49.170
...is not someone I need to go easy on.

07:51.280 --> 07:54.300
Which of these two will become Queen?

07:54.640 --> 07:57.890
We begin with Challenger Serena's performance!

08:00.080 --> 08:01.370
Serena, do your best!

08:01.590 --> 08:04.670
Please, God! I'll even stop snitching food off the plate before meals.

08:08.830 --> 08:09.640
Serena...

08:10.060 --> 08:11.990
You're also carrying our dreams on our behalf, so...

08:12.610 --> 08:13.520
...you can't lose this!

08:14.090 --> 08:15.620
It'll be fine... It'll be fine!

08:19.320 --> 08:20.180
All right, let's go!

08:32.750 --> 08:34.160
Tairenar, Flamethrower!

08:34.600 --> 08:36.290
Yancham, Dark Pulse!

08:43.050 --> 08:44.800
Nymphia, Swift!

08:59.930 --> 09:01.280
Go, Serena!

09:01.280 --> 09:03.660
Yancham, Tairenar, Nymphia!

09:03.660 --> 09:04.640
Good job!

09:26.810 --> 09:28.150
Everyone, let's go!

09:39.730 --> 09:40.880
Finish!

09:43.790 --> 09:45.340
We did as much as we could.

09:48.710 --> 09:49.710
Pokémon Quiz.

09:49.850 --> 09:50.650
The answer is...?

10:00.400 --> 10:03.640
Next comes the counter from the Kalos Queen:

10:04.050 --> 10:06.030
Performer Elle!

10:10.600 --> 10:13.430
Sorry, but <i>we</i> can't lose this either!

10:15.810 --> 10:17.800
Mafoxy, Mystical Fire!

10:18.250 --> 10:20.090
Vivillon, Psybeam!

10:26.600 --> 10:28.080
Frefuwan, Reflect!

10:41.710 --> 10:43.010
Elle-san's performance...

10:45.560 --> 10:48.000
...and Elle-san's smile gives everyone strength.

10:50.690 --> 10:51.210
I'm...

10:51.970 --> 10:53.970
...always on the receiving end...

10:59.150 --> 11:00.450
Finish!

11:00.690 --> 11:01.610
Awesome...

11:02.480 --> 11:03.800
She really is something.

11:04.300 --> 11:10.090
All right, both maidens have finished their beautiful and exciting performances.

11:10.670 --> 11:13.990
Everyone, please choose the Kalos Queen with your vote.

11:15.020 --> 11:16.570
Are you ready?

11:19.320 --> 11:19.830
Un,

11:20.700 --> 11:21.100
deux,

11:21.590 --> 11:22.480
trois!

11:23.520 --> 11:24.170
Trois!

11:25.390 --> 11:28.060
Will a new Kalos Queen be born?

11:28.590 --> 11:30.610
Or will the current Queen win once more?

11:31.260 --> 11:34.150
All right, this is the fateful moment!

11:48.750 --> 11:50.890
The glorious Kalos Queen is...

11:52.270 --> 11:53.690
...Performer Elle!

11:54.040 --> 11:56.730
She has defended her title of Queen!

11:59.320 --> 12:01.100
Too bad... It's Elle-san.

12:01.530 --> 12:04.080
She gave it her all. There is nothing that can be done about it.

12:04.620 --> 12:06.550
Her dream is still far from over!

12:07.040 --> 12:07.420
No!

12:11.630 --> 12:15.360
For her brilliant victory, Elle will be presented with the title of Kalos Queen...

12:15.360 --> 12:17.800
...as well as this tiara!

12:27.350 --> 12:29.080
Elle-san really is amazing.

12:37.950 --> 12:38.440
Serena.

12:39.100 --> 12:40.040
That was fun, right?

12:40.790 --> 12:42.490
Let's stand on the same stage together again someday.

12:46.930 --> 12:47.330
Yes!

12:47.880 --> 12:51.570
I'll practice much more and make sure to surpass you, Elle-san!

12:52.170 --> 12:53.210
Bring it on!

12:56.410 --> 12:59.880
With that, the Tripokalon Master Class comes to a close.

13:00.530 --> 13:04.170
Who will be the next to challenge Kalos Queen Elle?

13:04.680 --> 13:09.150
Let's meet again at this beautiful and exciting stage someday.

13:09.660 --> 13:12.010
Au revoir!

13:14.050 --> 13:14.600
All right.

13:15.010 --> 13:16.110
This should do.

13:16.570 --> 13:17.740
Make sure to let it rest.

13:18.330 --> 13:18.610
Okay.

13:19.530 --> 13:20.760
Thank you very much.

13:21.580 --> 13:22.270
Get well soon.

13:23.770 --> 13:24.610
How is your injury?

13:26.250 --> 13:27.280
It'll be fine now.

13:27.690 --> 13:28.730
Thank you very m-

13:28.390 --> 13:30.200
Don't ever be so reckless again.

13:30.730 --> 13:31.150
Huh?

13:32.010 --> 13:33.990
If you really want to defeat Elle, that is.

13:36.290 --> 13:37.370
You're right.

13:38.650 --> 13:43.010
As you said, Yashio-san, I wasn't able to win against Elle-san.

13:44.910 --> 13:46.840
When I watched Elle-san's performance earlier, I think I realized...

13:48.440 --> 13:51.980
...what Elle-san has and I don't.

13:52.940 --> 13:54.120
I'm inexperienced...

13:54.810 --> 13:57.890
...and I get saved by my friends and Pokémon all the time.

13:59.260 --> 14:00.390
But Elle-san...

14:01.030 --> 14:02.380
...makes people smile and...

14:02.830 --> 14:05.270
...gave advice to me, who was a complete stranger to her at the time.

14:05.950 --> 14:07.490
She's a person who can <i>give</i>.

14:09.010 --> 14:11.260
Until now, I've done nothing but receive from others, but...

14:12.120 --> 14:15.950
...I want to become Queen and give something <i>back</i> to people out there.

14:16.870 --> 14:18.000
I want to give them strength,

14:18.650 --> 14:19.490
make them smile,

14:19.840 --> 14:22.710
give them advice and sometimes scold them.

14:23.480 --> 14:25.820
That's why I need to work much harder still...

14:26.470 --> 14:28.170
...in order to become a good Queen.

14:30.170 --> 14:33.720
As long as you understand that, you can become a good Performer.

14:35.730 --> 14:37.100
Will you come with me?

14:39.520 --> 14:40.810
What do you mean?

14:41.350 --> 14:42.600
I will teach you everything...

14:43.030 --> 14:44.770
...about being a Performer.

14:45.920 --> 14:49.730
You don't need to answer right away, so think it through carefully before deciding.

15:03.570 --> 15:05.630
Serena, you were so close...

15:05.980 --> 15:09.150
Yeah. You'd all entrusted your dreams to me, yet I still lost...

15:09.150 --> 15:10.430
What are you talking about?

15:10.970 --> 15:13.350
From here on, we'll take a new step forward!

15:13.900 --> 15:18.000
I'll think of all kinds of new performances to surprise everyone with!

15:18.540 --> 15:20.380
I won't fall behind either, no matter what!

15:20.380 --> 15:21.520
Yeah, neither will I!

15:22.490 --> 15:24.910
Make some progress in <i>that</i> department too.

15:27.310 --> 15:28.530
Millefeui!

15:29.770 --> 15:31.570
See you! You guys take care too, Satoshi!

15:32.890 --> 15:34.000
You guys too.

15:34.590 --> 15:35.800
Let's meet on the stage.

15:36.350 --> 15:37.580
Let's go, Muchul!

15:41.500 --> 15:42.780
See you, guys!

15:44.380 --> 15:46.890
Yeah, say hi to Tierno and Trova for me too.

15:46.890 --> 15:47.700
Bye-bye!

15:47.700 --> 15:49.190
Let us meet again!

15:54.080 --> 15:54.870
All right then...

15:54.870 --> 15:55.210
Yes?

15:55.210 --> 15:56.190
Yes?

15:56.190 --> 15:58.220
Let's eat something delicious today!

15:58.670 --> 15:59.430
Huh?

15:59.430 --> 16:01.040
Aren't you upset?

16:01.040 --> 16:04.790
Of course not. It's thanks to you that I've made it this far in the first place.

16:05.090 --> 16:07.160
Well, I guess I'm gratefUlgamoth.

16:07.390 --> 16:08.840
M-Musashi!

16:10.390 --> 16:12.530
Musashi!

16:12.930 --> 16:14.050
What's with you?! Creeps!

16:14.050 --> 16:16.040
We'll follow you anywhere, Musashi-sama!

16:16.040 --> 16:17.340
This is going to be <i>your</i> treat, Kojiro!

16:17.340 --> 16:18.680
I'll pay! I'll so pay!

16:18.680 --> 16:20.330
I will, too!

16:23.070 --> 16:25.290
In the finals, I went for broke and ended up breaking.

16:26.190 --> 16:28.380
You gave it your all, so it's fine.

16:29.430 --> 16:31.340
As long as you start running toward your next destination.

16:31.880 --> 16:32.190
Yeah!

16:34.860 --> 16:35.880
All right, I'm off.

16:36.320 --> 16:38.640
Right now, it's just Sihorn and Yayakoma watching the house.

16:39.250 --> 16:39.950
Mama!

16:40.450 --> 16:41.020
Hm?

16:43.900 --> 16:45.640
No, it's nothing.

16:46.370 --> 16:47.610
All right. See you, then.

16:48.830 --> 16:49.800
Bye-bye!

16:49.800 --> 16:50.800
Please take care.

16:50.800 --> 16:51.820
Goodbye!

17:02.440 --> 17:03.650
What's up? Does it hurt?

17:04.120 --> 17:06.640
No. There was just something I had to think about.

17:07.180 --> 17:08.150
Oh, I see.

17:08.670 --> 17:11.280
Your next performance, maybe?

17:11.790 --> 17:13.470
Yeah, something like that.

17:13.470 --> 17:16.470
I get it. It's the same with me: When I lose a battle,

17:16.470 --> 17:18.280
I think about how I'll battle next time,

17:18.640 --> 17:20.390
and think, "I'll win next time!",

17:20.390 --> 17:21.810
getting all excited.

17:22.040 --> 17:24.460
Satoshi, it's amazing how you're always so optimistic.

17:25.120 --> 17:25.690
You think so?

17:29.230 --> 17:31.410
You'd never feel unsure about what to do, Satoshi.

17:33.800 --> 17:36.170
I feel unsure sometimes too.

17:37.640 --> 17:38.090
But you see,

17:39.790 --> 17:41.250
if you have time to feel unsure,

17:41.750 --> 17:42.840
you should just try making a move.

17:43.410 --> 17:45.790
If that ends in a failure, you'll still be left with <i>something</i>.

17:46.540 --> 17:48.060
There's nothing you could do that'd be pointless.

17:49.310 --> 17:50.060
Satoshi...

17:51.320 --> 17:52.170
Come on, let's go to sleep.

17:52.780 --> 17:54.430
We have to wake up early tomorrow.

17:56.250 --> 17:56.560
Yeah.

18:08.270 --> 18:09.000
Yashio-san!

18:14.210 --> 18:15.610
Oh, you're up early.

18:16.590 --> 18:17.990
I hope your answer is positive.

18:19.720 --> 18:20.390
Uhm...

18:20.860 --> 18:22.840
I'm very glad you invited me.

18:25.510 --> 18:27.290
But right now, I can't come with you.

18:28.010 --> 18:28.960
I'm sorry!

18:29.920 --> 18:30.960
May I ask why?

18:31.590 --> 18:33.170
I don't think it's a bad offer...

18:33.790 --> 18:36.490
I know it's an extremely gracious offer.

18:37.210 --> 18:43.940
But I don't think it'd be good for me if I left my journey with Satoshi and the others unfinished and went with you, Yashio-san.

18:44.400 --> 18:45.810
Are they friends of yours?

18:47.500 --> 18:51.440
At first I only started a journey because I wanted to leave the house,

18:53.750 --> 18:55.590
but then I discovered the path of being a Performer...

18:57.810 --> 18:58.610
...and met my rivals...

18:59.660 --> 19:00.730
...and Elle-san.

19:04.120 --> 19:07.710
I want to discover what lies ahead with my own eyes.

19:11.720 --> 19:13.480
I want to follow through with my journey till the end,

19:14.280 --> 19:16.120
and when I find an answer I'm satisfied with,

19:16.940 --> 19:17.630
then I'll...!

19:23.570 --> 19:24.210
Fine.

19:25.560 --> 19:27.930
Press forward until you're satisfied with yourself.

19:28.550 --> 19:30.540
And once you're satisfied,

19:31.130 --> 19:32.480
call this number.

19:43.040 --> 19:49.910
There will be a break next week. The next episode will air Thursday April 7th at 6:55pm!

19:45.170 --> 19:46.910
It's your turn next, Satoshi.

19:47.260 --> 19:48.970
Yeah, at the Eisetsu Gym.

19:49.230 --> 19:50.210
We'll win!

19:50.210 --> 19:51.210
We'll do some special training!

19:51.040 --> 19:55.910
Note that the broadcast time is changing starting April!!

19:51.970 --> 19:54.130
I will be with you the whole way.

19:54.530 --> 19:56.250
You're so motivated, Satoshi!

19:56.590 --> 19:57.130
Yeah!

19:58.680 --> 19:58.960
Yeah.

19:59.760 --> 20:01.050
I can't fall behind!

20:02.150 --> 20:07.640
Serena's Master Class challenge ended at the last hurdle when she couldn't match Elle.

20:08.240 --> 20:09.970
But there is still a long road up ahead.

20:10.480 --> 20:13.180
The path to become Kalos Queen has only just started.

20:16.030 --> 20:20.990
Pokémon no Uchi Atsumaru?

20:16.030 --> 20:20.990
Sunday March 27th at 8am

20:16.870 --> 20:19.320
Pokénchi will have a Pokémon Battle Special!

20:17.360 --> 20:20.990
Pokémon Battle
Ultimate Men's Playoff

20:19.320 --> 20:20.700
On Sunday at 8am!

21:44.970 --> 21:47.390
Performer News!

21:47.660 --> 21:51.000
Performer Communication is being brought to you right from the venue, where the excitement is still lingering!

21:51.280 --> 21:53.770
This time, we have a Master Class special!

21:53.770 --> 21:55.250
It is presented to you by me, Takuro, and...

21:55.250 --> 21:56.370
...me, Yajiko!

21:56.370 --> 21:59.340
Now that the tournaments have safely come to an end, this will be the final episode of this show as well.

21:59.340 --> 22:01.960
It seemed so long, yet was so short. Youth has that same innocence!

22:01.960 --> 22:05.800
It was a good tournament which showed many instances of the bond between Pokémon and Performer.

22:05.800 --> 22:08.640
Oh my! Hey... My eyes are tickling... They're tickling..

22:08.640 --> 22:10.170
What are you crying about?!

22:10.450 --> 22:13.360
Your ugly face... will become even uglier!

22:13.360 --> 22:15.760
I don't get what you're saying, but you're getting Circle Throw'd for that!

22:15.760 --> 22:17.660
Just throw me! Throw me!

22:18.140 --> 22:20.970
Finally, we'll finish this with a special collaboration show!

22:20.970 --> 22:22.900
These are the ones that will put on the show!

